From 572b211d57ef06d2228f8f637f3a4fb38097036f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:51:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): write each Fanuc-family length word with a decimal
 point

The Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Doosan DNM and Fanuc lathe posts wrote a
whole-number length with no point (Z14). A control with parameter
3401#0 DPI=0 reads such a word in least increments (0.014 mm), so a
rapid could go almost to Z0. Each length, angle, thread lead and
feed-per-rev word now has its point (Z14.). Macro-B constants, the
G76 P/Q and G83 Q words and feeds per minute do not change.

Pinned by crates/post/tests/decimal_point_fanuc_family.rs. The
goldens of these posts are regenerated; each diff only adds a point.

Fixes #1836

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
